  [3] Pollard, T., Moody, B. E., Lehman, L., Gow, B., Fernandes, C., Xie, C.,
      Johnson, A., Mark, R. G., & Heldt, T. (2026). PhysioNet as a global
      platform for biomedical research. Nature Health.
      https://doi.org/10.1038/s44360-026-00096-z

How this repository uses the data:

  * The recordings are NOT included in this repository and are not
    redistributed. tools/download_mitdb.py downloads them from PhysioNet into
    data/mitdb/, which is excluded from git.
  * Only derived results are published here (tables and charts in results/).
    The changes made to the data are listed at the top of safebeat/realdata.py:
    channel MLII, resampled 360 Hz to 250 Hz, per-record amplitude
    normalisation, cut into 10 s windows, labelled from the cardiologists'
    rhythm annotations ("(N" regular, "(AFIB" irregular), all other rhythms and
    the four paced records (102, 104, 107, 217) skipped.
  * The authors and PhysioNet do not endorse this project or its results.

